Production failures in `src/` must throw `AppError` from `src/errors/appError.ts` (or a subclass). Do not throw bare `Error`. Each failure needs a stable `code` (`<domain>.<reason_snake>`), a technical `message` (why/what/how for logs), `context` as `JsonObject` from `src/util/jsonValue.ts`, and `cause?: Error` when wrapping. In `catch`, use `error instanceof Error ? toAppError(error, { code }) : nonErrorThrown(code)`. Do not pass non-Errors to `toAppError`. Domain classes (`WebhookParseError`, `StaleHeadPushError`, `WorkItemPayloadValidationError`) keep their names for `instanceof`. Never put `AppError.message` on PR-facing surfaces. Use separate plain-English constants. Prefer `errorLogFields` / `serializeAppError` when logging.
